[00:00.67]Lesson 10 | 第10课
[00:02.03]Silicon valley | 硅谷
[00:08.14]What does the computer industry thrive on apart from anarchy? | 除了无政府状态，计算机工业还靠什么兴旺发达？
[00:14.59]Technology trends may push Silicon Valley back to the future. | 技术趋势也许会把硅谷推回到未来。
[00:19.04]Carver Mead, a pioneer in integrated circuits and a professor of computer science at the California Institute of Technology, notes there are now workstations that enable engineers to design, test and produce chips right on their desks, much the way and editor creates a newsletter on a Macintosh. | 卡弗·米德——集成电路的先驱、加州理工学院的计算机科学教授——指出，现在有些工作站使工程师可以在办公桌上设计、测试和生产芯片，就像编辑在麦金塔电脑上制作时事通讯一样。
[00:41.88]As the time and cost of making a chip drop to a few days and a few hundred dollars, engineers may soon be free to let their imaginations soar without being penalized by expensive failures. | 随着制造一块芯片的时间和成本降至几天和几百美元，工程师们很快就可以放开想像力，而不必因代价高昂的失败而受罚。
[00:55.03]Mead predicts that inventors will be able to perfect powerful customized chips over a weekend at the office -- | 米德预言，发明者将能在办公室里花一个周末的时间完善功能强大的定制芯片——
[01:02.31]spawning a new generation of garage start-ups and giving the U. S.  a jump on its foreign rivals in getting new products to market fast. | 从而孕育出新一代车库创业公司，并使美国在把新产品快速推向市场方面抢先于外国对手。
[01:13.10]'We've got more garages with smart people,' Mead observes. 'We really thrive on anarchy. ' | “我们有更多的装满聪明人的车库，”米德说，“我们真的是靠无政府状态兴旺发达。”
[01:20.92]And on Asians. Already, orientals and Asian Americans constitute the majority of the engineering staffs at many Valley firms. | 还有靠亚洲人。目前，东方人和亚裔美国人已构成许多硅谷公司工程技术队伍的多数。
[01:31.09]And Chinese, Korean, Filipino and Indian engineers are graduating in droves from California's colleges. | 而华裔、韩裔、菲律宾裔和印度裔工程师正成群结队地从加州的大学毕业。
[01:40.09]As the heads of next-generation start-ups, these Asian innovators can draw on customs and languages to forge tighter links with crucial Pacific Rim markets. | 作为下一代创业公司的头头，这些亚洲革新者可以借助自己的习俗和语言，同至关重要的环太平洋市场建立更紧密的联系。
[01:52.17]For instance, Alex Au, a Stanford Ph. D. from Hong Kong, has set up a Taiwan factory to challenge Japan's near lock on the memory-chip market. | 例如，来自香港的斯坦福大学博士亚历克斯·奥已在台湾建厂，向日本在存储芯片市场上近乎垄断的地位发起挑战。
[02:04.52]India-born N. Damodar Reddy's tiny California company reopened an AT&T chip plant in Kansas City last spring with financing from the state of Missouri. | 出生于印度的N.达莫达尔·雷迪，其设在加州的小公司去年春天在密苏里州的资助下，重新启用了堪萨斯城的一家美国电话电报公司芯片厂。
[02:17.26]Before it becomes a retirement village, Silicon Valley may prove a classroom for building a global business. | 在变成退休者村落之前，硅谷或许会成为一座讲授如何建设全球性商业的课堂。
